<body>
  <h1>Vida Terrestre i Biodiversitat</h1>
  <h2>Protegir la vida a la Terra</h2>

  <section>
    <p>
      SDG 15 aims to <strong>protect, restore and promote sustainable use of terrestrial ecosystems, sustainably manage forests, combat desertification, halt and reverse land degradation, and halt biodiversity loss</strong>.
      Healthy ecosystems are essential for human well-being and survival. Protecting life on land is critical for addressing climate change, ensuring food security, and preserving clean water sources.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h3>Key Targets of SDG 15:</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>15.1: Conserve terrestrial and freshwater ecosystems and their services.</li>
      <li>15.2: Promote sustainable management of all types of forests, halt deforestation, and restore degraded forests.</li>
      <li>15.3: Combat desertification and restore degraded land and soil.</li>
      <li>15.4: Ensure the conservation of mountain ecosystems and their biodiversity.</li>
      <li>15.5: Take urgent action to reduce degradation of natural habitats, halt the loss of biodiversity, and protect threatened species.</li>
      <li>15.6: Promote fair sharing of benefits from genetic resources and access to them.</li>
      <li>15.7: Combat poaching and trafficking of protected species.</li>
      <li>15.8: Introduce measures to prevent invasive alien species.</li>
      <li>15.9: Integrate ecosystem and biodiversity values into national and local planning.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h3>Why It Matters</h3>
    <p>
      Forests and ecosystems are the lungs of our planet. They provide food, clean water, and habitat for millions of species.
      Biodiversity underpins life on Earth and supports human health, livelihoods, and economies. Protecting life on land ensures a healthy future for all.
    </p>
  </section>
